+  Evidence: Probed _tools/_is_bash_entry against forms a YAML runtime honours; all carry a real Bash grant and report can_take_lock=False: YAML block list (parses to ['- Read'] — `\s*` eats the newline), double-quoted scalar ('Bash"'), single-quoted item, quoted flow item ('"Bash"'), trailing `# comment` ('Bash # registry'). `tools: [Read, Bash]` IS handled via .strip("[]"). Under-detection fails loud in the AC-2 direction but is a HOLLOW PASS for AC-4, whose test is literally named test_planner_tools_has_no_bash_entry_in_any_form. Mitigation found: test_parses_real_agent_tools_lines pins planner's exact parsed list and kills all five — so the privilege guarantee rests on a parser smoke-test, not on the privilege pin.
