+  Evidence: No secrets, no dependency changes, no new network or filesystem surface, no path traversal (KIT_ROOT is derived from __file__ and every agent path comes from AGENT_DIR.glob or a literal — no external input reaches a path). The arbitrary-code-execution basis for rejecting fix 1 is ACCURATE, verified from source: flock_edit.sh takes TARGET="$1", requires a literal `--`, then executes the remaining argv verbatim at :29 and :83 with no allowlist and no restriction to bash; registry_edit.sh:30 forwards everything via `exec bash ... flock_edit.sh "$ROOT/$FILE" "$@"`; and the documented usage at registry_edit.sh:9-10 is literally `-- bash -c '<update command>'`. A prefix-scoped grant on either wrapper therefore matches any argv beginning with that prefix, making it arbitrary code execution wearing a narrow-looking prefix. AC-5 is satisfied and substantively answered.
